# The status panel's active unit (StatusWin_draw_active, see statuswin.c): the picture, name and stats of the unit on the square,
# and the lines under them: the faction (for another's unit), the stats and abilities, the morale, home base, moves, flight turns,
# cargo, damage, orders. A stack of three units (ids 6 to 8, scout patrols of the player's faction) is made on the first unit's
# square, unit 6 is picked (the panel's sel_veh, 0x8c6b24), and the units' fields are changed with pokes; the unit table is at
# 0x952828, 0x34 a unit, so unit 6 is at 0x952960 (+4 the state, +0xc the faction in the high half, +0x10 damage and order, +0x24 the
# turns flown in the second byte, +0x28 the moves spent, +0x2c the home base in the high half). The prototype's words are at
# 0x9ab868 + 0x34 * id (proto 0 here: +0x20 the abilities, +0x24 chassis, weapon, armor and reactor, +0x28 carry, cost, plan, group).
